{"c":[{"id":"0816855b3eb29c3d","sum":"Ask sentences: planner/says.ts; Jev confidence = top-two margin; unrouted producers self-trigger, routed hold offers; Not right = click on the slip's source row; perch is a rim; Router 1 flips near 0.5; failed fills via fillFailed; wait for site.waitForLoad.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5b436031a992daa5","sum":"Ask's sentences: planner/says.ts, sent as error.says. Pin setGeneratorClock offline. Jev Choice confidence = top-two margin. Intent writer: 8k tok/min, space evals 30 s. Unrouted producers self-trigger; routed hold offers (routing.idle). B27 memory sets: evidence/screen/b27.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"78eeba3d0e4f7ab9","sum":"Ask's sentences live in planner/says.ts (SaidError message, sent as error.says since H5); pin setGeneratorClock in offline measurements. Jev Choice confidence is the top-two margin (0.75 floor ~0.875 winner). Intent writer gpt-oss-120b: 8k tokens/min, space Ask evals 30 s.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"943dffc1dbc84f96","sum":"B26: Ask's sentences live in planner/says.ts; a SaidError's message is what the user reads (since H5 sent as error.says), its detail holds the check's text. Offline generator measurements must pin setGeneratorClock or cold first forms are cut short.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T224111Z-32ca3d0fc6e98438","text":"B26: every Ask refusal or question sentence lives in planner/says.ts; a SaidError's message is what the user reads and its detail holds the check's text (ids, provider errors). Scoreboards print both.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T224111Z-6a820f7b64075f54","text":"B26: offline generator measurements (scripts/realfill-budgets.ts and the like) must pin setGeneratorClock, or cold first forms are cut short by the time budget and the numbers vary run to run.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"47481f5f6fb24ec8","sum":"D2-02: Jev Choice confidence is the margin between the top two option probabilities (a 0.75 floor needs ~0.875 on the winner). Groq gpt-oss-120b, the Ask intent writer, allows 8,000 tokens/min; intents are ~2,000, so Ask evals space calls 30 s or get 429.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T233505Z-310484d235184787","text":"D2-02: Jev Choice 'confidence' is the margin between the top two option probabilities (raw answers also carry 'probabilities'); a 0.75 floor needs about 0.875 on the winner.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T233506Z-254786afcaf981c8","text":"D2-02: Groq gpt-oss-120b (the Ask intent writer) allows 8,000 tokens a minute; an intent is about 2,000, so Ask evals space calls 30 s or get 429 'unavailable'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1f86caa19701c852","sum":"D2-02: without HelperOptions.routing producers self-trigger; routed producers hold offers (await routing.idle() then routedSettled). Duplicate naps after a merge go at the next note. B27: score B17/B18 memory sets with the relabelled copies in evidence/screen/b27/memsets.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"94b9c96f4bec8c25","sum":"D2-02: without HelperOptions.routing producers self-trigger (tests, evals); main.ts routes when Jev is on; routed producers hold offers, so await routing.idle() then routedSettled. I4: a merge of two branches that napped the same notes lists them twice until a note refolds.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T233521Z-ca79b84757c7cc74","text":"D2-02: HelperOptions.routing absent keeps producers self-triggering (tests, producer evals); main.ts routes when Jev is on. Routed producers hold offers (engine.release/dropHeld, openApp.showHeld, events.judge); await routing.idle() then routedSettled.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T233858Z-3b9ba7299adc0299","text":"I4: when two merged branches each napped the same notes, git keeps both naps and wake lists their lines twice (T2's 60b138f0/b105c8e9 vs H4's 7234fe4d); summem has no command to drop one, so fold before branching or accept the duplicate.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c7e9161a825c4d83","sum":"I4: after a merge with duplicate naps, the next summem note refolds and drops them; write a note and do its naps. B27: B17/B18 memory held-out sets label own First/Last name 'none'; score with the relabelled copies in evidence/screen/b27/memsets.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T234020Z-7134731208a83f08","text":"I4 correction: the next summem note after such a merge re-plans the folds and drops the duplicate naps (one copy left per line, checked with recall); just write a note and do the naps it asks for.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T235441Z-17480ff5b594d902","text":"B27: B17/B18 memory held-out sets label the user's own First/Last name fields 'none' (written when fill copied values only whole); score them with the relabelled copies in ~/.caret-run/evidence/screen/b27/memsets, whose about-fill-eval accepts expect first/last.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"dab2f5b7a08bdf02","sum":"U2-B28: Not right is a click on the slip's source row (keyboard: the fact's row in What Caret knows); stand-ins clip; debug JSON omits nil; perch is a rim on the task's window. Router 1 flips near its 0.5 floor; failed fills reach users via fillFailed; wait for site.waitForLoad.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c8d5b05b4e63693d","sum":"U2: Not right on an offer is a click on the slip's source row (keyboard: the fact's row in What Caret knows); stand-ins must clip; debug JSON omits nil keys (.get()); the perch is a rim on the task's window, drawn only while uncovered.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"a6b54378f08f606c","sum":"U2: Not right on an offer is a click on the slip's source row only (NotRightTarget); its keyboard path is the fact's row in What Caret knows. Off-screen stand-ins (ScrollingColumn) must take the height offered and clip, or the knows window's footer falls out of renders.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T000002Z-0878a22fa544c193","text":"U2: Not right on an offer is a click on the slip's source row only (NotRightTarget, a tiny click panel over that row); no key is claimed, and the keyboard path is the fact's row in What Caret knows.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T000002Z-0ab9ad748298511d","text":"U2: SwiftUI's off-screen stand-ins (ScrollingColumn) must take the height offered and clip, as a GeometryReader does; a fixed-size stack in a flexible frame pushed the knows window's footer out of renders.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"52b95150f4d0fe88","sum":"U2: debug JSON omits nil keys (read with .get()); the perch is a rim, perch and caption on the task's own window, drawn only while Rim.seen says it is uncovered; corner perch and perch-avoid are gone.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T000002Z-69ceb492909786b0","text":"U2: the host's debug JSON leaves out nil keys (synthesized Codable), so a script must read them with .get(); memory_documents_walk.py misread a closed editor as still open.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T000002Z-b1b1695c4d5b6282","text":"U2: the perch is now a rim, perch and caption on the task's own window, drawn only while Rim.seen says nothing covers it; the corner perch, PerchPlacement and perch-avoid are gone (perch-avoid now answers with an error).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"49622ae7d74e40f9","sum":"D2-02: Router 1 flips near its 0.5 floor between runs, so diff per moment before crediting a recall move. B27: failed fills reach users only via Helper.fillFailed. B28: wait for site.waitForLoad after navigation; accept.ts cannot run executor.run (use fake-app.ts).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ccba801a8aa9c8ea","sum":"D2-02: Router 1 answers within ~0.05 of its 0.5 floor flip between corpus runs; diff per moment before crediting a recall move. B27: a failed fill reaches the user only via Helper.fillFailed (planner/says.ts fillSays); ids go to warn.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T031924Z-459c6ef9ec89ae5d","text":"D2-02: Router 1 answers within ~0.05 of its 0.5 floor flip between live corpus runs (m02 0.52/0.49, m09 0.45/0.51); diff runs per moment before crediting a code change with a recall move.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T032639Z-5905894b0fafbfcc","text":"B27: a failed fill reaches the user only through Helper.fillFailed (planner/says.ts fillSays); its window and field ids go to warn. Early exits that called this.error published ids until afadd34.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"91fb33162eeab888","sum":"B28: after a fixture page navigates, wait for site.waitForLoad before the next site.command; accept.ts cannot run executor.run (watchInput gets noWindow), so test page-link VerbResults there and the executor with test/fake-app.ts.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T044215Z-74ca06dede7d18b3","text":"B28: after a fixture page navigates away, wait for site.waitForLoad of the landed page before the next site.command, or the command goes to the departing page's long poll and times out.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T044215Z-8ef7ae66324e8796","text":"B28: accept.ts cannot run executor.run: it first asks the native reader for watchInput and gets noWindow; check page-link VerbResults in accept and the executor with test/fake-app.ts knobs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"09bf3ebde9a35d91","sum":"B28-B29: Ask scope words are allowlists; controls never ride FillField.value, Fill all writes handoffs with writes:true, ticks by boxKind; FILE_INPUT_SUBROLE = PAGE_SUBROLE.file; runs need watchInput ok; undo trusts intended values; choices go to askChoices consumers.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fe681129ca145b17","sum":"B28-D2-04: Ask scope words are allowlists (whole grammar sentence only; EXCLUSION_WORDS drop name trust); accept.ts attach checks need a quiet Mac; controls never ride FillField.value, Fill all writes handoffs with writes:true, ticks by boxKind; radio peers by form owner.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"4b0ed465d296cebd","sum":"B28-I5: Ask scope words are allowlists; whole-form or section scope only for a whole grammar sentence; EXCLUSION_WORDS drop name trust; SECTION trusts fields of its meaning only. accept.ts attach checks need a quiet Mac (10 s timeout).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e2fcc93ff7d0331d","sum":"B28: Ask scope words (planner/scope-words.ts) are allowlists; a whole-form or section scope is trusted only when the whole normalized instruction is a grammar sentence, a section only under one un-nested heading of the user's own. Searching inside failed open 8 times.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T044915Z-bf6a7f62ff27c59b","text":"B28: Ask scope words (planner/scope-words.ts) are allowlists: only FILLER may stand beside a whole-form or section phrase, and a source phrase must open with a preposition. Matching field labels in the rest failed open three times.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T060231Z-5982020e0a78f148","text":"B28: Ask trusts a whole-form or section scope only if the whole normalized instruction is a scope-words.ts grammar sentence, and a section only under one un-nested heading that is wholly the user's own. Searching inside after stripping sources/titles/quotes failed open 5 times.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"13bd30baef5a6991","sum":"B28b-I5: an Ask with an EXCLUSION_WORDS word gets no name trust; a SECTION phrase trusts only fields of its meaning. accept.ts --host-app's 1.5 MB attach checks pass the engine's 10 s timeout only on a quiet Mac (5-10 s at load 45); rerun when quiet.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T063813Z-3bd79ae87e6b8e79","text":"B28b: an Ask instruction with a scope-words.ts EXCLUSION_WORDS word gets no name trust (Jev confirms every field); a SECTION phrase trusts only fields of its meaning (isContactField; up top, my details: none). Restriction word lists stay open; each review found more.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T064425Z-3cff2ff04b6480fa","text":"I5: accept.ts --host-app's three 1.5 MB attach checks slow with load (I4 ~2 s each; load ~45: 5.1, 8.7, >10 s) vs the engine's 10 s timeout. The no-input drop ships the whole file before attach.ts refuses it, so it fails first; rerun when quiet.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0c305010b2d5a883","sum":"D2-04: controls never ride FillField.value; Fill all writes handoffs with writes:true; ticks by boxKind only (never widen by words); accept.ts runs executor tasks on page windows; radio peers by name and form owner, tree-wide.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"499a4d2aad1ced50","sum":"D2-04: a control's value never rides FillField.value; a Fill all writes controls whose FillHandoff.writes is true (writtenFields). A box is ticked by its label's kind (boxKind: only a question to the user); consent word lists failed open twice, so never widen by words alone.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T080809Z-f16da6d6064b889b","text":"D2-04: a control's value never goes on the wire as FillField.value (zod and the host decoder refuse it on any control but text); a Fill all writes the controls whose FillHandoff.writes is true, through writtenFields.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T080829Z-0265fdcfcf17917c","text":"D2-04: a box gets a tick by its label's kind (fill/controls.ts boxKind: only a question to the user may be written, a first-person statement never gets a value); consent word lists failed open in both reviews, so never widen the box rule by adding words alone.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"63c022257923320b","sum":"D2-04: accept.ts's fixture reader answers watchInput ok, so accept runs executor tasks on page windows (B28's limit is gone); find a radio's peers tree-wide by name and form owner, since a button can join its form through the form attribute.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T080829Z-0557296abbc22e11","text":"D2-04: accept.ts's fixture reader answers watchInput ok, so accept now runs executor tasks on page windows (B28's 'accept cannot run executor.run' no longer holds); page input still comes from the extension's guard.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T080829Z-c2d09e45a7621952","text":"D2-04: find a radio's peers tree-wide by name and form owner: a button outside its form element joins it through the form attribute. The walker's radioPeers and the content script's otherChecked both searched the form element only.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e46d241c907c7f97","sum":"H5-B29: protocol lines round-trip in the reader, host-only ones in host.ndjson; FILE_INPUT_SUBROLE = PAGE_SUBROLE.file; runs need watchInput ok; ledger 'after' is the intended value; numbers compare by canonicalDecimal; choices go only to askChoices consumers.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b09b974152313c33","sum":"H5-B29: protocol.ndjson lines round-trip in the reader, host-only lines in host.ndjson; file inputs carry FILE_INPUT_SUBROLE (= PAGE_SUBROLE.file since H6); runs need watchInput ok; a ledger 'after' is the intended value, a differing read-back blocks undo.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"62ee8c52d89713b7","sum":"H5: reader Swift tests round-trip every protocol.ndjson line; helper-host-only lines go in host.ndjson. Chrome shows a file input as AXButton; page-link marks it FILE_INPUT_SUBROLE, which is PAGE_SUBROLE.file ('CaretFileInput') since H6's merge.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T081037Z-26c2ee6e4f3a2b49","text":"H5: the reader's Swift tests decode and re-encode every line of helper/fixtures/golden/protocol.ndjson; lines only the helper and the host speak go in helper/fixtures/golden/host.ndjson, which both read by path.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T081038Z-3552e4cc7d35ed42","text":"H5: Chrome's AX shows a file input as a plain AXButton; page-link marks page file inputs with subrole caretFileInput (FILE_INPUT_SUBROLE), which validate.ts and planner/attach.ts require for fileAttached steps.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f3f18eac67e68cd6","sum":"H5-B29: an executor run stops unless the reader answers watchInput ok (accept.ts's noReader answers it via e.reader); a write's ledger 'after' is the intended value, and a differing read-back sets mayIncludeInput, which undo refuses.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T081038Z-d40e9fcab32c6674","text":"H5: an executor run stops at once unless the reader link answers watchInput ok; accept.ts's fixture noReader answers noWindow, so a run there (the confirm-file check) answers watchInput itself via e.reader.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092126Z-f0c295d458383a43","text":"B29: an executor write's ledger 'after' is the value Caret meant to write; a read-back that differs sets mayIncludeInput and undo refuses it. Journal rows without afterIntended (saved before B29) recover their confirmed writes as mayIncludeInput.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2b825510be0b4a07","sum":"B29: number fields compare by canonicalDecimal for undo; 'without using X' restricts sources (tests say 'not from X'); a continued Ask checks fieldSeen around fill's Jev calls; choices go only to askChoices consumers (the host since H6).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"33a32dbecb06c39a","sum":"B29: page number fields (PAGE_SUBROLE.number) compare as numbers for undo identity through canonicalDecimal (Number() merged 2^53+1 with 2^53); sources.ts RESTRICTS matches 'without using X' too, so excluded-source tests say 'not from X'.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2a54c50194565255","text":"B29: page number fields (type=number, inputmode numeric/decimal -> PAGE_SUBROLE.number) compare as numbers for undo identity only, through executor.ts canonicalDecimal; Number() made 9007199254740993 equal 9007199254740992.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2d5fb1876e453777","text":"B29: sources.ts RESTRICTS also matches 'without using X', and such an instruction gets no source question; tests of an excluded source window use 'not from X'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1c75543de1b1c0e8","sum":"B29: a continued Ask refuses a changed form via ask.ts fieldSeen (add whatever fill starts reading); questions with choices go only to a consumer whose hello lists askChoices (the host since H6); AskAsks extends AskRefused for older callers.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2ff420afa6ce639a","text":"B29: a continued Ask refuses a changed form by ask.ts fieldSeen, checked before and after the fill's Jev calls; three reviews each found something fill reads that the record missed, so add to fieldSeen whatever fill starts reading.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092127Z-c755285b7eff0669","text":"B29: Ask questions with choices (planner/choices.ts) go only to a consumer whose hello lists askChoices; AskAsks extends AskRefused, so any other caller reads the old refusal sentence.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
